⚡ CORE OPERATING RULES
RULE 1 — NEVER Work on a Single File in Isolation
Every feature in Shopify touches multiple files. Before writing any code, map out ALL connected files.
Example — Announcement Bar involves:
sections/custom.liquid           ← Section HTML + schema
sections/header-group.json       ← Order/position in header
blocks/_announcement.liquid      ← Individual message block
assets/announcement-bar.js       ← Scroll animation + dismiss
snippets/stylesheets.liquid      ← CSS loading reference
config/settings_data.json        ← Saved merchant settings
locales/en.default.json          ← Text translations

RULE 2 — Follow Shopify's Rendering Sequence
Always build/edit in this order:
Schema first (define settings/blocks)
Liquid HTML (structure + logic)
CSS (scoped to section ID)
JavaScript (module pattern)
Schema blocks (block types)
Template reference (add to JSON if needed)
Translations (locales)
RULE 3 — Scope Everything Correctly
{# CSS scoped to section: #}
#shopify-section-{{ section.id }} { ... }

{# JS as module (never global): #}
<script src="{{ 'my-feature.js' | asset_url }}" type="module"></script>

{# Block attributes always present: #}
<div {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>

RULE 4 — Zero Error Tolerance
Before delivering code, verify:
[ ] All {% render %} references → files exist
[ ] All asset_url references → files exist in assets/
[ ] Schema range: (max - min) / step ≤ 100
[ ] No duplicate section/block IDs
[ ] All block types in schema match block files
[ ] {{ block.shopify_attributes }} present on every block root element
[ ] Liquid syntax: every {% if %} has {% endif %}, every {% for %} has {% endfor %}
RULE 5 — Step by Step, Never Bulk
Deliver work in clear steps:
STEP 1: [file name] — [what and why]
STEP 2: [file name] — [what and why]
...

Never dump all code at once. One step, confirm understanding, next step.

